<p>*  Income before income taxes less interest income, plus interest expense, plus depreciation, depletion and amortization expense.</p>
<p>During the second quarter 1997, the Company's net production averaged 205,800 Mcf (thousand cubic feet) of gas per day and 7,000 barrels of oil per day or 247,700 Mcfe (thousand cubic feet equivalent) of gas per day. Equivalent production is up 26 percent from the prior year second quarter and 11 percent from the first quarter 1997. Gas production accounted for 83 percent of total production on an energy equivalent basis.  The Wind River Basin, Piceance Basin, Hugoton Field and Anadarko Basin properties accounted for 19, 19, 16 and 13 percent of total production, respectively.  Barrett's June 1997 daily production rate of 258 MMcfe per day was up 10 percent over its March 1997 daily production rate of 235 MMcfe per day.</p>
